{
  "fields": {
    "schema-version": "1"
  },
  "item-count": 6,
  "schema-version": 1,
  "sections": {
    "context": "`MemoryStore` (`src/store.ts`) keeps one bucket per series name in a `Map`,\nand `IngestQueue` (`src/ingest.ts`) already bounds *samples per series* via\n`maxSamples`/`maxPerSeries` — an existing series can never grow past its cap.\nNothing bounds the number of distinct series keys, though: `series()` accepts\nany string that passes `isValidSeries` (`src/validate.ts`), and each new,\nnever-seen-before name opens a fresh bucket in the map. A caller that mints a\nnew series name per request — a bug that folds a request id, a user id, or any\nother high-cardinality value into the series name — grows `buckets` by one\nentry per sample forever; nothing ever prunes an *entry*, only the *contents*\nof entries older than the retention window (and `prune()` only deletes a\nbucket once every sample in it has aged out, which never happens for a series\nthat keeps receiving new, unique labels). The process runs out of memory with\nno warning beforehand.\n\nThe fix is a cap on the store's total series count, analogous to the existing\nper-series sample cap. What happens at that cap is a real design choice (which\nof two costs to pay: refuse a new series, or evict an existing one to make\nroom) and is recorded as a decision during implementation, not settled here.\n\nNon-goals: this does not change per-series behavior (`maxSamples` and the\ningest queue's own overflow policy are untouched), does not add persistence\nor cross-process coordination, and does not attempt to detect *which* label is\nthe runaway one — only to keep the total bounded regardless of cause. Expected\nto touch `src/store.ts` (the cap and its enforcement), `src/config.ts` (a new\nenv-configured limit alongside the existing ones), and `src/index.ts` (wiring\nthe new config value into `MemoryStore`'s constructor).",
    "criteria": [
      {
        "id": "store-takes-a-maximum-series",
        "statement": "`MemoryStore` is constructed with a maximum number of distinct series it\nwill hold, validated the same way as the existing `maxPerSeries` cap (a\npositive integer; anything else throws at construction).",
        "title": "Store takes a maximum series count"
      },
      {
        "id": "cap-is-configurable-from",
        "statement": "`Config`/`loadConfig` (`src/config.ts`) grows a new positive-integer field,\nread from its own environment variable with a sensible default, following\nthe same present-but-invalid-fails-loud rule as `ROLLUP_WINDOW_MS`,\n`ROLLUP_MAX_SAMPLES`, and `ROLLUP_RETENTION_MS`; `src/index.ts` wires it into\nthe `MemoryStore` constructor.",
        "title": "Cap is configurable from the environment"
      },
      {
        "id": "cap-is-enforced-at-admission",
        "statement": "Once the store holds that many distinct series, a sample for a series not\nalready tracked is handled per the recorded overflow decision (rejected\noutright, or admitted by evicting an existing series) — the store never\nsilently exceeds the configured series count.",
        "title": "Cap is enforced at admission"
      },
      {
        "id": "existing-series-are-unaffected",
        "statement": "A sample for a series the store already tracks is accepted exactly as\nbefore regardless of total series count or the cap's overflow policy —\nthe cap governs *admitting a new series*, not writes to one already held.",
        "title": "Existing series are unaffected by the cap"
      },
      {
        "id": "overflow-is-observable",
        "statement": "The store exposes a counter (mirroring `IngestQueue.droppedCount()`) so an\noperator can see that the series cap has been hit, distinct from the\nexisting per-series sample-drop counter.",
        "title": "Overflow is observable"
      },
      {
        "id": "freed-capacity-is-reusable",
        "statement": "Once `prune()` removes a series' last sample and its bucket is deleted, that\nfreed slot is available to a subsequent new series — the cap bounds the\nstore's *current* series count, not a lifetime total.",
        "title": "Freed capacity is reusable"
      }
    ],
    "goal": "Bound the number of distinct series `MemoryStore` will hold at once, so a\nsingle mislabeled or runaway series name cannot grow the store's key space —\nand therefore its memory — without limit."
  },
  "slug": "bound-total-series-cardinality",
  "staged": "bound-the-total-number",
  "type": "spec"
}

