content.content:
{
  "fields": {
    "cites": [
      "adr:reject-the-newest-sample-when",
      "adr:keep-the-sample-store",
      "adr:reject-a-new-series-once"
    ],
    "schema-version": "1"
  },
  "item-count": 6,
  "schema-version": 1,
  "sections": {
    "components": [
      {
        "description": "The single admission gate for a `Sample`: a lowercase, dotted-path series name,\na finite numeric value, and a non-negative integer timestamp. Every other\ncomponent may assume a `Sample` it holds is well-formed — validation happens\nonce, here, not again downstream.",
        "id": "validation",
        "implemented-by": "src/validate.ts#validateSample",
        "title": "Validation"
      },
      {
        "description": "Parses wire-format lines (`<series> <value> [<at>]`) into samples, and buffers\nthem in a bounded FIFO sized by `ROLLUP_MAX_SAMPLES`. On overflow it drops the\noldest buffered sample rather than refusing the newest — see\nadr:reject-the-newest-sample-when — and counts the drops via\n`droppedCount()`. As of this writing `IngestQueue` is constructed and drained\nby `Service.tick()` but nothing calls `push()` on it: the live HTTP ingest path\n(`Router`) writes to the store directly, bypassing this buffer entirely.",
        "id": "ingest",
        "implemented-by": "src/ingest.ts#IngestQueue",
        "title": "Ingest"
      },
      {
        "description": "Holds samples in one timestamp-sorted bucket per series, capped per series at\n`ROLLUP_MAX_SAMPLES` (oldest trimmed on insert) and capped in total distinct\nseries at `ROLLUP_MAX_SERIES` — a sample for a series not yet tracked is\nrejected once that cap is hit, counted via `rejectedSeriesCount()`, and an\nalready-tracked series is never evicted to make room (adr:reject-a-new-series-once).\nDeliberately non-durable (adr:keep-the-sample-store): a restart loses\neverything held. `range()` answers windowed queries, `series()` lists what is\ncurrently held, and `prune()` drops samples older than a cutoff, deleting a\nseries' bucket entirely once it is empty.",
        "id": "store",
        "implemented-by": "src/store.ts#MemoryStore",
        "title": "Store"
      },
      {
        "description": "Reads a series' recent samples out of the store and buckets them into\nfixed-width windows aligned to multiples of `ROLLUP_WINDOW_MS`; a window with\nno samples is omitted rather than reported as a zero measurement. Each window\ncollapses to `{count, mean, min, max}`, and `formatSummary` renders that into\nthe plain-text line the HTTP API returns.",
        "id": "rollup-and-summary",
        "implemented-by": "src/rollup.ts#rollup",
        "title": "Rollup and summary"
      },
      {
        "description": "A transport-agnostic method+path dispatcher over the store: `POST /samples`\nparses and writes each wire line straight into `MemoryStore` (stopping at the\nfirst invalid line, reporting how many landed before it); `GET /series` lists\ntracked series; `GET /summary/<series>` rolls up and formats the trailing\n`ROLLUP_RETENTION_MS` window at `ROLLUP_WINDOW_MS` granularity. Taking plain\nstrings in and a plain reply object out keeps it testable without binding a\nsocket.",
        "id": "router",
        "implemented-by": "src/router.ts#Router",
        "title": "Router"
      },
      {
        "description": "The one place real implementations get chosen: `createService` reads `Config`\nfrom the environment, constructs the queue, store, and router with it, and\nreturns a `tick()` that drains the queue into the store and prunes anything\nolder than retention. Everything it wires is injectable (a `Clock`, a\n`Config`) so the rest of the system never reaches for ambient state itself.",
        "id": "service-wiring",
        "implemented-by": "src/index.ts#createService",
        "title": "Service wiring"
      }
    ],
    "overview": "This service is a bounded, in-memory rollup buffer over a recent window of\ntime-series samples (`Sample { series, value, at }`, validated in\n`src/validate.ts`). Three concerns sit between the wire and an answer to\n\"what has series X looked like recently\": admitting samples, holding them,\nand turning what's held into a summary. `src/index.ts` wires the three\ntogether and drives the maintenance loop that connects them.\n\nThe write path has a documented split that the current wiring does not\nfollow in practice: `Router.dispatch`'s `POST /samples` handler\n(`src/router.ts`) parses each wire line and calls `MemoryStore.put`\ndirectly — it never touches `IngestQueue`. The queue is fully implemented,\nconstructed by `createService`, and drained every `tick()`, but nothing in\nthe current code path ever calls `IngestQueue.push`, so the queue as wired\ntoday is inert: `tick()`'s drain-then-prune is really just a periodic prune.\nThis document describes the queue's own behavior for when it *is* on a\nwrite path (or for a future one), but flags the gap plainly rather than\nimplying the HTTP route is buffered by it."
  },
  "slug": "ingest-store-and-rollup",
  "staged": "document-how-ingest-store-and",
  "type": "arch-doc"
}

